  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>Right behind Toulon's train station, Parc de Lices spreads over 90,000 m² of green space in the heart of the city, with a dedicated dog park and an agility area confirmed by the City of Toulon. Plenty of room for your dog to stretch its legs on a proper long walk, without having to leave the urban area. Lead required, free and open access.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>The exact opening hours differ between sources: one lists 9am-9pm in July-August, another 9am-7pm "depending on the season" — check on site or on toulon.fr before planning a visit late in the day.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: take advantage of the park's wide open spaces for a longer walk than a stroll around the block, especially during the day when there's more foot traffic.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>Toulon's train station and town centre are right nearby, handy for combining the walk with other stops during the day.</p>
